  "timeframe": "Last 14 days ending 2026-11-11T19:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "Identify volumes whose peak IOPS/throughput approach provisioned limits (e.g. >70-80%), gp2 volumes with low or depleting BurstBalance, high VolumeQueueLength, and instance-level EBS bandwidth/IOPS limits being hit (EC2 EBSReadOps/EBSIOBalance%/EBSByteBalance% where relevant). Check whether alarms exist for volume status/health (VolumeStatus / StatusCheckFailed related), BurstBalance, queue length, and capacity (disk used percent via CWAgent if present); list which production-looking volumes have no alarms. Return a concise findings list with volume IDs, severity (high/medium/low), and brief supporting numbers. Keep output compact."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS performance headroom and alarm coverage"}], "created_at": null}

